  "caveats": [
    "Artificial 32x32 two-mark A-B-A' sequences; supervised on the same update pattern; no natural-image generalization",
    "Original 1792-byte checkpoints came from an earlier matched 500-step training run; data generation, held-out generator and objective match",
    "Half-budget models use matched parameters but graph transport costs more compute than vector",
    "Wide gain-only graph uses 16 channels and more trainable parameters, distinct from the same-parameter gain-only 896B control",
    "Gain-only cannot represent negative/oscillatory couplings; signed-real learned transport remains an untested alternative to complex phase",
    "No loop-holonomy or gauge invariant training and propagation is dissipative, not unitary"
  ]
